== Trivia ==
* This item is similar to {{i|Doctor's Remote}}, which fires one missile per use.
* In the original game it was possible to control the crosshair with the mouse. This was removed in Rebirth.
** {{dlc|r}} Mouse control can however be re-enabled by editing the <code>options.ini</code> file in <code>C:\Users\<username>\Documents\My Games\Binding of Isaac Afterbirth/Rebirth</code> and changing the line <code>MouseControl=0</code> into <code>MouseControl=1</code>. Also useful for {{I|The Ludovico Technique}}.
* The {{I|Dr. Fetus}} and Epic Fetus items are based off of [[supermeatboy:Dr. Fetus|Dr. Fetus]], the main antagonist in [[wikipedia:Super Meat Boy|Super Meat Boy]] which is a game by Edmund McMillen (the creator of The ''Binding of Isaac: Rebirth'').
* In Wrath of the Lamb, Epic Fetus could be found in both the Secret Room and Treasure Room item pools.
** {{dlc|r}}Epic Fetus was added to the Secret Room item pool.
* This item is used in {{chal|Glass Cannon}}.
* In ''Wrath of the Lamb'', this item was originally unlocked by beating a challenge titled, "The Doctor's Revenge!".

